  "id": "trovo_alpujarreno",
  "name": "Trovo (Alpujarra improvised sung verse)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "The trovo is improvised verse in quintillas delivered in turn by two or more troveros who answer and taunt one another. In the Alpujarra of Granada and Almería the verses are sung to a fandango-derived tune that violin, guitar and bandurria play between them; a related tradition flourished in Cartagena and its mining district, where José María Marín was its best-known trovero.",
  "recipe": "classic modern trovo, ballad Poetry, Mediterranean ballad branch. solo with instrumental accompaniment, single lead single track no stacking. fiddle, classical nylon-string guitar, bandurria. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
